\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, these eyes have never seen
\par That radiant form of Thine;
\par The veil of sense hangs dark between
\par Thy blessed face and mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I see Thee not, I hear Thee not,
\par Yet art Thy oft with me;
\par And earth hath ne'er so dear a spot,
\par As where I meet with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Like some bright dream that comes unsought,
\par When slumbers o'er me roll,
\par Thy image ever fills my thought,
\par And charms my ravished soul.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yet, though I have not seen, and still
\par Must rest in faith alone;
\par I love Thee, dearest Lord, and will,
\par Unseen but not unknown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When death these mortal eyes shall seal,
\par And still this throbbing heart,
\par The rending veil shall Thee reveal
\par All glorious as Thou art.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

